# Render-repo .gitignore — used ONLY when staging a run to the shared cloud
# render repo (emotionmedialab/video-renderer). Unlike the template's own
# .gitignore, the MEDIA must be committed so the CI runner can render it.
# When staging (Stage 7), copy this over the run's .gitignore:
#     cp render.gitignore .gitignore
node_modules/
out/
# comp-frames.json is now COMMITTED when staging: the plan job reads it instead of
# spending ~750 MB of cold setup to recompute one integer. Generate it at staging:
#   node scripts/comp-frames.mjs <CompId> comp-frames.json
*.log

# ⚠️ CREDENTIALS. This file REPLACES the run's own .gitignore at staging, so any
# `.env` rule that lived there is gone the moment you `cp render.gitignore
# .gitignore`. Without these lines the Pexels/Jamendo key is force-added into a
# SHARED render repo. Caught pre-commit on the ivonescimab long-form, 2026-08-22.
.env
.env.*
sil.txt

# never stage: the pre-boost VO, the raw bed/clip sources and local working files.
# (They lived only in staged copies until 2026-10-17; `git add -f public/vo` would still force vo.src.mp3 in,
# so force-add media by FILE, or delete vo.src.mp3 from the stage copy.)
public/vo/vo.src.mp3
_src/
rms.txt
